  there is a known bug in pre-3.0 nethack sources that will end your game
with a "panic" death. typically the bug triggers a "freeinv" error when you
drop many items of different types (i.e. D!= to drop potions and rings).
the work-around (short of fixing the sources) is to remember to only drop
one type of item at a time or drop all items (i.e. D! or D= or Da are ok).
"panic" deaths have a "panic" saved-game file associated with them. the
"panic" saved-game file has the name of a normal saved-game file with a
".e" appended. at least on unix systems, if you can access the "panic" file
you can "rebuild the dungeon" by simply removing the ".e" extension and
replaying. it is probably safe to assume that this bug has been fixed in
nethack3.0 which is rumored to be "ready, real soon now". perhaps in a
month or two you could upgrade along with the rest of us ...

